            {
              "id": "c5a0a201-7540-36c5-93d0-f80f5853bbfb",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlapping memory regions between the source and destination in the memory copy operation. The source and destination may refer to overlapping areas in memory, as indicated by the data flow analysis. Additionally, the source pointer may be null, which could also lead to undefined behavior. There are no explicit checks or guards in the code to prevent these issues. The classification and verdict both indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue that should be addressed to prevent potential memory corruption or crashes.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory regions that may overlap, add a runtime check to ensure the source and destination do not overlap before calling the memory copy function. If overlap is possible, use a safe copying strategy such as copying to a temporary buffer or using a function that handles overlap safely.\n\n```cpp\n// Example runtime check for overlap\nchar *dst_ptr = reinterpret_cast<char*>(&sections);\nchar *src_ptr = reinterpret_cast<char*>((int32_t *) dst->op_params + 11);\nsize_t copy_size = sizeof(int) * 4;\nif (src_ptr + copy_size <= dst_ptr || dst_ptr + copy_size <= src_ptr) {\n    memcpy(dst_ptr, src_ptr, copy_size);\n} else {\n    // Handle overlap safely, e.g., use a temporary buffer\n    char temp[sizeof(int) * 4];\n    memcpy(temp, src_ptr, copy_size);\n    memcpy(dst_ptr, temp, copy_size);\n}\n```\n\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nAlternatively, if you know that the source and destination regions may overlap, replace the memory copy function with one that is defined for overlapping regions, such as memmove.\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(&sections, (int32_t *) dst->op_params + 11, sizeof(int)*4);\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [NIST Glossary: Buffer Overflow](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/buffer_overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS121708"
